[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138041,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Reactive hyperplasia of the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE) is a non-neoplastic proliferation of RPE cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138042,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138043,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9B7Y Other specified disorders of the retina</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138044,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> nodular hyperplasia of the retinal pigment epithelium.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> pseudoepitheliomatous hyperplasia; pseudoadenomatous hyperplasia; reactive hyperplastic lesion of the retinal pigment epithelium; ringschwiele.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138045,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138046,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Reactive hyperplasia of the RPE can occur anywhere in the retina {11782230}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138047,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>RPE hyperplasia is classified as localized, multifocal, or diffuse. It presents as darkly pigmented deposits. The pigment may be associated with retinal blood vessels, resulting in a spiculated appearance.</p>\r\n<p>Nodular reactive RPE hyperplasia can be confused with adenomatous RPE tumours or choroidal melanoma. On fluorescein angiography, reactive RPE hyperplasia shows early hypofluorescence, with areas of hyperfluorescence in the late phase. It shows high reflectivity on ultrasound {11782230}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138048,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The incidence is unknown. Reactive hyperplasia of the RPE can occur in patients of any age and either sex. Multifocal hyperplasia may be seen in older people.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138049,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of primary hyperplasia is unknown. Secondary hyperplasia can occur secondary to congenital abnormalities, inflammation, degenerative diseases, intoxications, radiation-induced choroiditis, chronic retinal detachment, subretinal haemorrhage, sequelae of traumatic retinopathy, or retinitis pigmentosa {5965122;11782230}. There may be a chronic vitreous base and zonular traction.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138050,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The proliferation of RPE cells is induced by growth factors.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138051,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138052,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Reactive RPE hyperplasia can range from simple duplication of cells to massive proliferations with intervening basement membrane material; in advanced, late-stage cases, the hyperplasia may be accompanied by collections of connective and osteoid tissue {5965122}.</p>\r\n<p>In nodular reactive proliferation of the RPE, the cells are arranged in a tubular pseudoadenomatous pattern, with a large amount of basement membrane&ndash;like material. Areas of extracellular material alternate with areas of cellular proliferation. Neoplastic features, mitotic figures, and necrosis are absent {5049451}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Reactive hyperplasia of the RPE must be distinguished from choroidal melanoma, RPE adenoma, RPE adenocarcinoma, congenital hypertrophy of the RPE, combined hamartoma of the retina and RPE, and simple hamartoma of the RPE.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
